From ae9003c0419a070694b15e5277e7307f0fadbb9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:22:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Line mode: one continuous bar over the avatar column

- Simple mode now draws a single bar from the top of the list to the bottom
  instead of one bar per avatar. It sits on the detected avatar column (the
  most common avatar x inside the list) and is as wide as the avatars, or the
  user's minimum thickness if that is larger.
- The bar is limited to the scrolling list: it stops below the top bar /
  pinned bar and above the message box or bottom navigation.
- Telegram: same single bar in the chat list; inside chats only in groups
  (private chats and channels start their bubbles at the left edge).
- No lag: scroll events no longer trigger a rescan in line mode, content
  changes are throttled to ~300 ms, the overlay only redraws when the line
  actually changes, and the column is remembered for a few seconds when no
  avatar is on screen.
- Dynamic circle mode keeps its per-avatar behaviour; items now carry their own
  shape so onDraw no longer reads preferences every frame.
